{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>A cistern.</b> In the sacred tongue it is feminine, and it is the flowing one. So too, 'the cistern' — its waters are choice. A בור is dug or excavated beneath the heavens. If so, the cistern is like a spring, and there is no need to mention the channel, and it will be a gathering of waters adjacent to a pit, for there is a pit that has no water. Some say that it is deficient of a vav, like ראובן, שמעון, שמש, ירח." "<b>And if it touches their carcass.</b> The waters touching their carcass will be unclean."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes a fragment resembling a phrase about choice waters; the allusion is compressed and rendered literally without expansion."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:37.739941596Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}